messages:
lisa: FYI opened a PR to consolidate structured-output examples for function calls and SDK snippets — https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/492

mike: looked quick — nice cleanup. can we include a small migration note for teams using the old tool-caller v1? some customers still call the old shape. :eyes:

lisa: yes, planning a short section titled 'Migrating from legacy tool-caller' with example diffs. sara, can you own node SDK snippets? i added python already.

sara: on it. will add node example + a lightweight parse_fallback helper. also found a broken link in the doc that points to /docs/integrations/old-tool. will update to /docs/function-calling/migration

mike: great. kevin can you sanity-check the JSON schema we currently show in the examples? i'm worried about leaning on required too much.

kevin: quick read — we should avoid marking nested subfields as required unless they're guaranteed. recommend using oneOf for union payloads and a short note about validators returning clear errors. e.g.:

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "action": {"type": "string"},
    "payload": {
      "oneOf": [
        {"$ref": "#/definitions/create"},
        {"$ref": "#/definitions/lookup"}
      ]
    }
  },
  "required": ["action"]
}
```

ben: also add an example of a malformed model response and a parse fallback we recommend. customers hit silent failures when the model emits unexpected keys. small snippet suggestion:

```js
// parseFallback: try parse, fallback to regex/heuristic + log to Sentry
function parseWithFallback(text) {
  try {
    return JSON.parse(text);
  } catch(e) {
    // fallback: simple kv extractor
    const m = /action:\s*(\w+)/i.exec(text);
    return m ? {action: m[1], fallback: true} : null;
  }
}
```

sara: putting that fallback into node SDK example. do we want to include a small test harness in docs that asserts canonical examples parse? would help catch regressions during PRs.

lisa: yes please. add a snapshot test + a CI check that loads the example prompt set and runs parseWithFallback, fail on null. minimal, quick to run.

mike: also tagging docs-ops: can we run a link sweep before merging? i flagged 3 other internal links while editing. @doc-bot any chance of an automated link-check on preview?

doc-bot: docs preview deployed: https://preview.docs.redwood.ai/pr-492 — link-check job queued (job id 7832).

kevin: one more: guardrail wording — let's avoid making it sound like we can perfectly enforce output shape. suggest phrasing: 'Use schema + parsing checks to detect drift; prefer safe fallbacks and clear telemetry.'

lisa: reworded in PR. removed strong language. added a short table of recommended actions: schema validation, token limits, fallback parsers, and eval sets.

ben: for migration note, include a compact diff example so integrators can update quickly. something like:

```diff
- tools: [{name: 'search', input_schema: {q: 'string'}}]
+ functions: [{name: 'search', input_schema: {query: 'string'}}]
```

sara: pushed node examples + migration snippet. also fixed that broken link and updated TOC ordering.

mike: i'll review tonight. if all good, we can merge tomorrow morning and run the docs-ops sweep. :shipit:

lisa: thanks everyone. after merge i'll add the quick-release note for customers on Slack + update the SDK CHANGELOG with the parse helper mention.

doc-bot: merge-ready check: all checks passing except one flaky example test (CI #1297). marking for manual review.

kevin: i'll take the flaky test — looks like nondeterministic whitespace in one example. trivial fix.

lisa: perfect. plan: kevin fixes test, mike merges, doc-bot runs final sweep, then release note. low-risk, high-clarity change. :tada:
